{# Widget: a rich text panel beside the block's own text.

   Carries `iw-block__text` like every other rich text of the bundle: that is
   the class the variant paints its paragraph surface on, so a widget text sits
   on the same ground as the text zone next to it instead of on nothing at all.
   Without it a theme with a paragraph background and light text left this one
   panel unreadable.

   `iw-widget__text` stays alongside it: nothing in the bundle styles it, but it
   is the hook a project would have used to target this panel specifically. #}
{% if text is defined and text is not empty %}
    <div class="iw-widget__text iw-block__text prose max-w-none {% if paragraphRadius is defined and paragraphRadius %}{{ paragraphRadius }}{% endif %}">
        {{ text|raw }}
    </div>
{% endif %}
